            <ArticleTitle>[A man with a painful elbow].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A7777</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 54-year old man presented with unremitting pain in the left dorsolateral forearm, despite postural advice and glucocorticoid injections. Electromyography and MRI did not show any abnormality. Based on a clinical suspected radial tunnel syndrome, operative decompression was performed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
